# ── Secrets — NEVER commit ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds IMAP credentials, the notification token, the IDFM/PRIM API key and the
# RFR income figure. `.env.example` is the committed template. See CLAUDE.md hard rule 7.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
# Local criteria overrides. `config/rent/criteria.json` is committed and deliberately carries only
# values that were already public; `criteria.local.json` is where real budget, ranked communes and
# any private tuning go, and it overrides the committed file field by field (Q11). Four documents
# claimed this file was gitignored while nothing ignored it — a `git add .` after tuning would have
# committed the developer's real criteria to a public repo. Verify with:
#   git check-ignore -v config/rent/criteria.local.json
/config/*/*.local.json

# ── Runtime state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The seen-set and the listings DB. Deleting these makes the next run RE-NOTIFY
# EVERYTHING and loses price history for good — see CLAUDE.md § "Credentials & stateful data".
seen.json
# The default RENT_SCOUT_DB location. Deliberately NOT under /var/, which is documented two blocks
# down as container-lifetime scratch — the seen-set is the opposite of scratch.
/state/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# WAL sidecars. They exist only between a write and a clean close — i.e. after a crash or a
# reclaimed container, which is exactly when someone runs `git add .` to salvage work. They hold
# un-checkpointed pages, including adapter error text.
*.sq3
*.sq3-wal
*.sq3-shm
*.sq3-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-journal

# ── Claude Code working state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reports and PreCompact handoffs. Container-lifetime by design: they survive
# compaction inside a session and die with the container. Never committed.
/var/
.claude/settings.json.bak*
.claude/settings.local.json
/claude-bundle/

# ── PHP ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# vendor/ holds only Composer's generated autoloader — this project has zero runtime
# dependencies. Regenerate with `composer install`.
/vendor/
/composer.lock
# The test runner is PHPUnit's official PHAR rather than a Composer dev dependency: this
# container's egress policy blocks GitHub dist zipballs, so Composer falls back to full git
# clones and vendor/ balloons to 2.6 GB for a test runner. See README.md § Getting started.
/tools/*.phar
# PHPUnit writes its per-test-duration cache beside whatever cwd it is run from, and the
# documented invocation is `php tools/phpunit.phar`. Untracked and unignored, it showed up
# in `git status` on every run — one more thing for a `git add -A` to sweep into a commit.
/tools/.phpunit.result.cache

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# ── Editors / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.orig
*.rej
*.log

